course: dictionary
lesson: 14863
title: The word ravage
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To ravage something is to damage or destroy it very badly. «The storm ravaged the coast.» The coast was not just a little scratched: the storm hit it hard and left a lot of harm behind.
explain: You will often meet ravage in history and geography. «The village was ravaged by fire.» «Floods ravaged the farmland.» Look at the words around it: fire, floods and war are clues that something terrible happened.
explain: Ravage can also be a noun, used with «of». «The ravages of time» means the damage that many years have done. «The old church showed the ravages of war.» Here it means the terrible marks something has left behind.
fact: Ravage is a verb. It means to damage or destroy something badly.
fact: Ravaged is the past form: «The forest was ravaged by fire.»
fact: Ravages is also a noun, usually with «of»: «the ravages of war».
fact: «The ravages of time» means the damage that many years have caused.
fact: Things that can ravage land include wars, fires, floods, diseases and pests.
exercise: «The flood ravaged the town.» What does ravaged mean here? | Painted bright blue | Cleaned carefully | Made very quiet | *Damaged badly
exercise: «The old city showed the ravages of time.» What are the ravages of time? | A holiday in the past | Hours spent playing games | The clocks in the city square | *The damage that many years have caused
exercise: «The fire ravaged the forest.» Find and copy the word that is the past form of ravage. | forest | fire | the | *ravaged
test: «Disease ravaged the crops, and the farmers lost their harvest.» What does ravaged mean? | Counted carefully | *Destroyed badly | Watered gently
test: In «the ravages of war», what do the ravages mean? | A type of weapon | *The terrible damage left by war | Happy memories of a party | The names of soldiers
exam: Which sentence uses ravage correctly? | *The storm ravaged the houses by the sea | The teacher ravaged the classroom with kindness | The gentle breeze ravaged the flowers | We ravaged a happy birthday song
